From be752dac85ef2f7c1e80af529adff96a75513c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeadingLight <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:06:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] LeadingLight's tools for its project agents

An embedded berthd gives its Claude and Codex agents an MCP server of LeadingLight's tools
(berthd mcp leadinglight). Each call goes through berthd to the app (POST /v1/ll/call), which
takes calls with GET /v1/ll/calls and answers them. A call never says who makes it: berthd
finds the agent's session from the process on the socket's other end (LOCAL_PEERPID). Reads
wait for the app and are refused when it isn't open. Writes are kept first (leadinglight/
outbox.json), with any evidence files copied as they are (leadinglight/files), and offered to
the app until it answers, so one made while the app is quit is taken when it next opens, and
one sent again is kept once.
